{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Full-suite run for this change: **12677 passed, 52 skipped, 1 failed** in 1061s.\n\nThe single failure is NOT caused by this change and is filed separately as `future-fibroid-hammerkop` (9151-907b-471d-4a38), linked `discovered_from` the same audit parent:\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count`\n\nGrounds for attributing it elsewhere:\n- this change touches ONLY `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`, and adds no import-time side effect and no cross-module state — a session fixture and a `functools.cache`, both confined to that module's namespace;\n- the failing test predates all four tickets in this batch (`4010da6493`, 'Decline removals of never-confirmed peer links') and is an ancestor of the base this batch branched from;\n- it PASSED in the two earlier full-suite runs of this same batch;\n- it passes in isolation (10 passed) and passes `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` under `-n 3 --dist worksteal` three consecutive times (2575 passed each).\n\nMechanism identified while triaging: the summary line the test asserts is emitted under `if declined:` in `apply_inbound_records.py`, and `declined` only increments when `confirm_store is not None`. With no confirm store the removal is still declined and still logged PER ITEM — which is exactly the message caplog held — but the summary never fires. So the ordering-sensitive input is `confirm_store` resolution. Details and acceptance criteria are on the new ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786610532833068001,"uuid":"6df0987a-a641-437c-9efe-bdf0ecf587f4"}